==== Asus Rescue Mode ====

For Windows users, Asus provide a Firmware Restoration Tool to restore original firmware to the RT-AC57U v1.  Download both the tool and the latest firmware for RT-AC57U v1 from here:
[[https://www.asus.com/Networking/RT-AC57U/HelpDesk_Download/|Asus download page]]

Instructions for using the tool is described here:
[[https://www.asus.com/uk/support/FAQ/1000814/|Restoration Tool instructions]]

The steps are summarised below:

  -  Download & Install the asus "Firmware Restoration" from asus website
  -  Download the factory image from asus
  -  Switch off the Router
  -  Hold Reset Button and switch on the Router
  -  Release button when front LED flashes slowly
  -  Use the following to set up your TCP/IP settings:IP address: 192.168.1.10 Subnet mask: 255.255.255.0
  -  Start the Firmware Restoration tool
  -  Select firmware *.trx and upload

Recommend to factory reset the router as follows:

  - Power on the router for a minute or two.
  - Hold the Reset button in for a few seconds.
  - When the Power LED starts to blink, release the button.
  - After the router reboots, the Asus web UI should present you with the Quick Setup Wizard.

